  "id": "P1-W02-M3",
  "title": "Three things kill a script. Each has exactly one defence.",
  "alt": "A backup.sh box in the centre attacked from three sides: an unquoted variable that word-splits into two tokens, two scheduled copies starting at the same time, and a SIGTERM arriving mid-write. Beside each attack the fix is drawn in green \u2014 quoting the variable, an atomic mkdir lock, and write-to-temp-then-rename. Below, a crossed-out trap for SIGKILL and a three-run idempotence checklist where runs two and three must change nothing.",
